            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.342,
            0.462,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13 Decision Theory"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.373,
            0.782,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a. ((ski (.08 win not-broken 100) (.02 win broken 50) (.72 not-win not-broken 0) (.18 not-win broken -50)) (not-ski (.2 broken -10) (.8 not-broken 0))"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.412,
            0.649,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "algorithm_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.213,
                0.412,
                0.649,
                0.428
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "b. "
                },
                {
                  "type": "equation_inline",
                  "content": "\\mathrm{U}(\\mathrm{ski}) = 8 + 1 + 0 + -9 = 0"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "; "
                },
                {
                  "type": "equation_inline",
                  "content": "\\mathrm{U}(\\mathrm{not~ski}) = -2"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "; so we ski!"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "sub_type": "algorithm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.437,
            0.784,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "c. Given perfect info about my leg, we have the tree ((0.2 broken ((ski (.1 win 50) (.9 not-win -50)) (not-ski -10))) (0.8 not-broken ((ski (.1 win 100) (.9 not-win 0)) (not-ski 0)))) which evaluates to ((0.2 broken ((ski -40) (not-ski -10))) (0.8 not-broken ((ski 10) (not-ski 0))) ((0.2 broken -10) (0.8 not-broken 10)) With perfect information I have expected utility -2 + 8 = 6. So expected value of perfect info is 6 - 0 = 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.537,
            0.784,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "d. Given perfect info about winning the race, we have the tree ((0.1 win ((ski (.2 broken 50) (.8 not-broken 100)) (not-ski (.2 broken -10) (.8 not-broken 0)))) (0.9 not-win ((ski (.2 broken -50) (.8 not-broken 0)) (not-ski (.2 broken -10) (.8 not-broken 0))))) which evaluates to ((0.1 win ((ski 90) (not-ski -2)) (0.9 not-win ((ski -10) (not-ski -2)))) which evaluates to ((0.1 win 90) (0.9 not-win -2)) = 9 - 1.8 = 7.2. So expected value of perfect info is 7.2 - 0 = 7.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.652,
            0.784,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "e. Yes. You just put the win branch after the broken branch, and use the conditional probabilities for win given broken."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.705,
            0.586,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14 Markov Decision Processes"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
